   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## A picture's palette + your own wheels\n\nTwo pictures in, as in template 08: **yours** (top) and a **colour source** (bottom). **Latent Color Match** starts the run in the source's palette; **Grade Wheels (latent)** takes its bearings from the model's first prediction — already in that palette — holds it while the model draws, and adds your adjustment on top. The circles here push the shadows towards teal and the highlights towards warm.\n\nThe lower sampler renders the same seed with the palette alone, so the two outputs show what the wheels add. Move a circle and run again: drag, Shift for fine moves, Alt-click to reset, right-click for presets.\n\n`denoise` 0.5 keeps your composition. Leave Latent Color Guidance and A1111 Color Correction out of this chain: both pull back towards the source and would take your adjustment with them."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
